            "id": "D",
            "text": "Breeding crops with higher levels of vitamins and minerals, or higher protein and healthier fat CASE STUDY Some strains of Bacillus thuringiensis produce protein that kill certain insects such as lepidopterans (tobacco budworm, armyworm), coleopterans (beetles) and dipterans (flies, mosquitoes). Bacillus thuringiensis forms protein crystals during a particular phase of their growth. These crystals contain a toxic insecticidal protein. The Bt toxin proteins exists as inactive protoxins but once an insect ingests the inactive toxin, it is converted into an active form due to alkaline pH of the gut which solubilise the crystals."
